@@ -1,3 +1,7 @@
+## 0.5.14 · 2026-11-14
+
+On-call guidance now follows the current rota and integration screens, and Gaps this week covers the same seven-day window as its timeline, including earlier uncovered hours. Restoring an archived administrator lets the owner confirm their name and keeps access working when they sign in again. The installer guidance runs checkpoint and move-in export scripts with rer’s supplied Node runtime, and compatible integration samples are ready to paste into a terminal with a privately configured key. Agent approvals and reviews explain coordination changes using people and service names; follow-up summaries correctly say that completion requires human review by default. Incident filters, timeline entries and Readiness use readable status labels. This patch includes a security fix for the deployed product: Vite 8.2.4 addresses launch-editor vulnerabilities. The pinned rer remains 0.2.113; this update adds no migration. Back up first, keep applied migrations unchanged and keep the existing pager active: paging stays OFF.
+
 ## 0.5.13 · 2026-11-13
 
 Local launch guidance now explains how to open Oncall from the terminal on your own computer and how to make rer available in later terminals. Archive exports show the data size on disk without treating it as the final archive size or estimating completion before the total is known. Restore rejects an archive that predates a recorded erasure before staging its contents. Agent policy-change events include the covered classes and a digest identifying the adopted policy document, without exposing its rules or call facts. This patch uses rer 0.2.113 and adds no migration. Back up first, keep applied migrations unchanged and keep the existing pager active: paging stays OFF.
